From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Elena Maher <12779416+elenaOnline@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 22:50:32 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] gpui: Add hidden and image cursors

CursorStyle only named the platform's cursors, so an app drawing its own
cursors (a canvas with rotated resize handles, say) could neither hide
the cursor over an element nor show an image, as CSS `cursor: none` and
`cursor: url(...)` do.

CursorStyle gets `None` and `Image(CursorImageId)`. The id stays Copy:
App::register_cursor_image takes a CursorImage (straight RGBA, scale
factor, hotspot in logical pixels) and returns the id, and
App::unregister_cursor_image forgets it. On macOS the image becomes an
NSCursor (an NSImage with a non-premultiplied NSBitmapImageRep) cached per
id on the main thread, set through the view's cursor rects like the
built-in cursors; None is a transparent cursor, so hiding stays per
hitbox and never touches [NSCursor hide]'s global count. The web backend
maps None to `none`; other backends show the arrow for both for now.
